                    r2_pct:                 `%`,
                    effort_anchor:          `Anchor & top 3 (defend the EUR 13M Aérospatiale relationship)`,
                    effort_midtier:         `22 high-margin mid-tier accounts (EUR 9.5M, growth headroom)`,
                    effort_longtail:        `Profitable long-tail (the rest of the book)`,
                    effort_small:           `40 loss-making small accounts (EUR 25k fabricators)`,
                    r2_smalltier_label:     `Service tier for the 40 loss-making small accounts.`,
                    r2_midtier_label:       `Service tier for the 22 high-potential mid-tier accounts.`,
                    tier_premium:           `Keep them on the same premium high-touch tier as everyone else — treat all customers equally`,
                    tier_growth:            `Move them to the mid “growth” tier — a partial trim`,
                    tier_selfserve:         `Move them to a low-cost self-serve / transactional tier — recover the EUR 1.1M leak`,
                    tier_transactional:     `Transactional / self-serve — cheapest, but they stay under-served`,
                    tier_growth2:           `A funded “growth” tier — proactive account management to unlock the headroom`,
                    tier_strategic:         `Full strategic-partner tier — the most expensive package, same as the anchor`,

                    r3_ai_label:            `Deploy ONE AI module well (the data only supports one this quarter).`,
                    r3_ai_hint:             `Deploying any single module reliably needs EUR 90k of data cleanup. Switching on all three spreads the same data and budget across three mediocre models you will trust none of.`,
                    r3_defense_label:       `Answer Aérospatiale's 9% cut + dedicated-engineer ultimatum.`,
                    r3_growth_label:        `Where do you find the revenue to replace the at-risk volume?`,
                    ai_all:                 `Switch on all three thinly — churn prediction, account scoring and next-best-action together`,
                    ai_churn:               `Churn prediction — flag at-risk accounts early (would have caught the Aérospatiale risk)`,
                    ai_scoring:             `Account scoring / prioritisation — re-segment the 180 accounts by value and potential`,
                    ai_nba:                 `Next-best-action prompts — lift share-of-wallet via guided cross-sell inside existing accounts`,
                    def_blanket:            `Match the 9% and extend it across the book “to be consistent” — keep everyone happy`,
                    def_cave:               `Give Aérospatiale the full 9% + free dedicated engineer, no strings — keep 100% of the account at any cost`,
                    def_volume:             `Targeted discount tied to a multi-year volume commitment; sell the engineer as a paid service`,
                    def_value:              `Value reframe — total cost of ownership, reliability, the engineer as a paid service; hold price`,
                    def_walkaway:           `Graceful partial walk-away — accept they dual-source 40%, keep the profitable 60%, redeploy the engineer`,
                    growth_newlogos:        `Chase new logos — win fresh accounts to replace the Aérospatiale risk`,
                    growth_mix:             `A mix of new logos and some cross-sell`,
                    growth_sow:             `Grow share-of-wallet inside existing top accounts (only ~35% captured today) before chasing cold logos`,

                    r4_target_label:        `Set a credible target share-of-wallet for the top accounts (%). Baseline ~35%.`,
                    r4_target_hint:         `An honest, reachable target (around 45–55%) you can hit via cross-sell beats a heroic number with no plan. Over-promising 70%+ with new logos will not land.`,
